// Nantian Gateway xDS Control-Plane Protocol
//
// This file defines the gRPC-based xDS (discovery service) contract between
// the Go control plane and Rust data plane. The control plane acts as the
// xDS management server, pushing configuration snapshots (listeners, routes,
// backends, secrets) to data-plane instances via bi-directional streaming.
//
// Protocol flow:
//   1. Data plane opens a StreamConfiguration RPC, sending a DiscoveryRequest
//      with its node identity and subscribed resource types.
//   2. Control plane responds with a DiscoveryResponse containing a full
//      ConfigSnapshot.
//   3. Data plane acknowledges (ACK) or rejects (NACK) the snapshot.
//   4. On any configuration change, the control plane pushes a new snapshot.
//   5. Data plane periodically reports health/readiness via ReportStatus.

